/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: Godot 4.5 dev 4\n\nNot reproducible in: Godot 4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev4 - Linux Mint 22.1 (Xia) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Intel(R) HD Graphics 4400 (HSW GT2) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i3-4160 CPU @ 3.60GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe max fps option should limit the fps to the set fps, however, even if the vsync mode  option is disabled, the fps does not show any limit.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a51db129-0888-46b2-9965-4633bfd8ddc1)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4ac65044-02f3-4604-9f5a-c5c759ae1c22)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4603bb4e-a042-4983-bd3c-3abc03390fc4)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/37c35652-ca71-4980-b98d-f9d9ce3415f2)\n\n\nSame project in godot 4.4.1\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a6a2c4c-edff-4fc9-bfc9-744891afee99)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new project\n2. Change the max fps option to 60 and change the vsync mode option to disabled\n3. create a 2D node\n4. Run the current scene\n\nThe monitors tab of the debugger panel will show that the fps goes up to more than 60 or whatever the maximum setting is.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"